	abstract = {This article presents a method that convexiﬁes state-constrained optimal control problems in the control-input space. The proposed method enables convex programming methods to ﬁnd the globally optimal solution even if costs and control constraints are nonconvex in control and convex in state, dynamics is nonafﬁne in control and convex in state, and state constraints are convex in state. Under the above conditions, generic methods do not guarantee to ﬁnd optimal solutions, but the proposed method does. The proposed approach is demonstrated in a 16-D navigation example.},
